# v08 silhouette-local shading v45

Source: /Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/PaintedCloud/v04/Altitude/Approved/T_CloudLook_RadialCrisp_v08. Source preserved.

Built-in image edit of original concept used as shading donor, aligned using v08 uniform_polar_fit 0.9756793933809876. Only R and corresponding B delta changed inside A>=128 cloud region within 96px Manhattan distance of threshold edge at 4096 resolution. Strength ramps from edge and fades into deep interior; 0.65 maximum weight with donor delta limited to ±24 before weighting. A and G copied unchanged. Alpha<128 and deep interior unchanged. Post-save readback: 2,834,009 changed R pixels; A/G differences 0; differences outside allowed band 0.

Import is packed linear vector displacement texture, not concept RGB. No level application. Engine appearance still needs user review; numerical preservation is not visual approval. Shade_Review.png displays R with original alpha.

## Image edit prompt

Local shading cleanup only for this existing polar cloud texture. Preserve all cloud locations, sizes, outer silhouettes, gaps, wisps and deep internal shading. Do not change style globally. Clean only the narrow region just INSIDE each cloud silhouette: merge noisy tiny alternating bright/dark flecks into connected natural light or midtone surfaces, remove rim-like dark/bright bands, no white drawn outline. Keep broad volume and original cloud detail farther inside intact. Do not introduce flat concentric bands, repetitive scallops or new brush marks. Inward-facing crowns remain luminous filled surfaces, outward undersides stay soft and subdued. No blur halo into black sky. No alpha erosion, no thickening or moving silhouettes. Grayscale on black, same square layout. Subtle local cleanup, not redesign.
